{
  "sn22.83:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.83 ",
  "sn22.83:0.2": "9. Senior Mendicants ",
  "sn22.83:0.3": "With Ānanda ",
  "sn22.83:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn22.83:1.2": "There Ānanda addressed the mendicants: ",
  "sn22.83:1.3": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "sn22.83:1.4": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "sn22.83:1.5": "Ānanda said this: ",
  "sn22.83:2.1": "“Reverends, the venerable named Puṇṇa son of Mantāṇī was very helpful to me when I was just ordained. ",
  "sn22.83:2.2": "He gave me this advice: ",
  "sn22.83:2.3": "‘Reverend Ānanda, the thought “I am” occurs because of grasping, not without grasping. ",
  "sn22.83:2.4": "Grasping what? ",
  "sn22.83:2.5": "The thought “I am” occurs because of grasping form, ",
  "sn22.83:2.6": "feeling, ",
  "sn22.83:2.7": "perception, ",
  "sn22.83:2.8": "choices, ",
  "sn22.83:2.9": "and consciousness, not without grasping. ",
  "sn22.83:3.1": "Suppose there was a woman or man who was young, youthful, and fond of adornments, and they check their own reflection in a clean bright mirror or a clear bowl of water. They’d look because of grasping, not without grasping. ",
  "sn22.83:3.2": "In the same way, the thought “I am” occurs because of grasping form, ",
  "sn22.83:3.3": "feeling, ",
  "sn22.83:3.4": "perception, ",
  "sn22.83:3.5": "choices, ",
  "sn22.83:3.6": "and consciousness, not without grasping. ",
  "sn22.83:4.1": "What do you think, Reverend Ānanda? ",
  "sn22.83:4.2": "Is form permanent or impermanent?’ ",
  